  "caveats": [
    "Pure intraday momentum (30m or 60m signal, flat overnight) cannot reach TQQQ's CAGR: TQQQ's drift is mostly overnight (30.2%/yr vs 5.9%/yr intraday).",
    "The first-hour effect is weak (t about 1.4-2.3) and not present in every year; 2019 and 2023 had positive afternoons after negative first hours.",
    "The strategy round-trips roughly 100 times per year; at 5bp the 10y CAGR falls from 55.6% to 43.5%.",
    "The max drawdown is the COVID crash (-44.6%, 2020-02-19..2020-04-13); an intraday signal cannot avoid overnight gap risk.",
    "TQQQ is a 3x daily-reset product with path dependence and end-of-day rebalancing flows (Cheng & Madhavan 2009); realized tracking and future flows may differ.",
    "No shorting, no leverage beyond 100% TQQQ; cash earns zero during afternoon exits."
  ]
